  "_integrationTestNotes": "ROOT-LEVEL ERROR END EVENTS (mergeRequestClosedError, devDeploymentError, stageDeploymentError, prodDeploymentError): these end with an uncaught error end event (codes 500/500) that raises a process-level error and creates an incident, so the instance never reaches IS_COMPLETED. CPT covers these by routing to the branch and asserting the error end event is reached with state IS_ACTIVE (the element sits active pending the incident) rather than asserting process completion or termination. LOOP-BACK 'no'/'else' FLOWS (splitCheckDevDeployment/Stage/Prod 'no', joinCheckMergeRequestStatus 'else'): covered by publishing a non-matching webhook first (different deployedFolder, or action=update) so the gateway routes the default flow and re-awaits the catch event, then publishing the matching webhook. The closed-MR path can still be verified via integration testing: publish a webhook with action=close and confirm the process raises an incident on mergeRequestClosedError. INTEGRATION NOTES — This process integrates with GitLab API (create branch, check file, update/create file, open merge request) and Camunda Web Modeler API (get token, get folder details, get file content, get/create milestones). Integration tests should: (1) use a real GitLab test repository; (2) use real Web Modeler API credentials; (3) verify the merge request is created with correct content; (4) verify milestones are created in Web Modeler; (5) verify successful deployment events trigger stage and prod deployment milestones. Key CPT patterns: openMergeRequest resultExpression sets createdMergeRequest (not mergeRequestId) — used as correlationKey for checkMergeRequestStatus webhook (977b3fd3..., correlationKey=createdMergeRequest.id). Deployment webhooks use static correlation keys (dev/stage/prod). manualQaTest is a native Zeebe user task (zeebe:userTask) — use COMPLETE_USER_TASK. splitAdditionalTasks is a parallel gateway — must complete all 3 paths: optionalTests, optionalBusinessOwnerVerification, and the direct path (handled automatically). PUBLISH_MESSAGE variables must match the resultExpression output (e.g. devDeploymentWebhookPayload) not raw request.body. Note: getFolderDetails must return folder.content.files array with items having an 'id' field (not 'fileId') since getFileContent uses file.id in URL. splitIsDmn routes BPMN files to getLatestMilestone (default path) and DMN files to endNoDmnMilestoneComparison (skip). getFileContent sets 'content' variable (via resultExpression header), not a nested 'file' object. The multi-instance sub-process runs per file: parallel fork (createMilestone + getFileContent), then getLatestMilestone (for BPMN), then splitHasMilestone (null → no comparison link needed)."
